.TH MGSH-CLI 1 "May 2026" "v2.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
mgsh-cli \- Model Context Protocol (MCP) interface for the Sovereign Mesh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mgsh-cli
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mgsh-cli
is a Go-based Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides a bridge between LLM-based agents and the Sovereign Mesh gRPC Control Bus. It operates via standard input/output (stdio) using JSON-RPC, allowing agents to discover and invoke mesh-native tools.
.SH PROTOCOL
The server implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP) version 2024-11-05. It responds to standard MCP methods:
.TP
\fBinitialize\fR
Exposes server capabilities and metadata.
.TP
\fBtools/list\fR
Returns a registry of all available mesh-native tools.
.TP
\fBtools/call\fR
Invokes a specific tool with provided arguments.
.SH TOOLS
The following tools are exposed by the server:
.TP
\fBremote_execute\fR
Execute a shell command on a mesh node.
.TP
\fBprovision_node\fR
Orchestrate multi-cloud node provisioning (GCP, HETZNER, AWS).
.TP
\fBget_starchart\fR
Retrieve unified mesh visualization (SVG) and accounting records.
.TP
\fBexecute_strike\fR
Execute high-priority strike protocol commands via PQR tickets.
.TP
\fBtrigger_training_cycle\fR
Trigger an autonomous training cycle for a Sovereign neural core.
.TP
\fBmonitor_neural_vitality\fR
Retrieve real-time metrics (Loss, Drift, Vitality) for an active session.
.TP
\fBregister_citizen\fR
Register an external entity as a Sovereign Citizen via CBC burn.
.TP
\fBrequest_city_service\fR
Provision autonomous digital infrastructure (DNS, Tunnel, Compute).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The server expects the Mesh Engine to be reachable at \fBlocalhost:1111\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
